<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Apache</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Apache are a group of culturally related Indigenous peoples of the American Southwest and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, speaking Southern Athabaskan languages. Arriving from the north by about 1500, they include the Chiricahua, Mescalero, Jicarilla, Lipan and Western Apache. For more than two centuries their raids challenged Spanish, Mexican and American frontier settlements, and leaders such as Cochise and Geronimo resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> until 1886.</p></div>
